---
description: One fact, one field. Do not store the same data twice on a type.
alwaysApply: true
---

# One source of truth

A class, struct, or record stores each fact once. Do not keep a second field, set, cache, or copy that restates data another member already owns.

Derive a lookup from the owner at the use site. Order, identity, and membership come from that one member.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — the list is the ids, and the set is the same ids again
readonly IReadOnlyList<string> idNames;
readonly HashSet<string> ids;
ids = [.. idNames];

// ✅ GOOD
readonly IReadOnlyList<string> ids;
public IReadOnlyList<string> Ids => ids;
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
readonly ids: readonly string[];
private readonly idSet = new Set(this.ids);

// ✅ GOOD
readonly ids: readonly string[];
this.ids.includes(col);
```

```rust
// ❌ BAD
id: Vec<String>,
ids: HashSet<String>,

// ✅ GOOD
ids: Vec<String>,
```
